{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["R13", "U8"],
      "pins": ["U8.1"],
      "nets": ["FB", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "On the Power sheet the AP63203WU (U8) feedback pin 1 is drawn on a net labelled 'FB' that carries a 51.1 kΩ resistor R13 to GND, sitting next to the L1/C9 output node that is labelled +3V3.",
      "expected": "The specification states the fixed-3.3 V AP63203WU has its FB pin tied directly to the +3V3 output and that 'no external feedback divider is needed', i.e. no resistor should sit on the FB node.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "FB(1) is tied directly to +3V3 ... so no external feedback divider is needed"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U8 AP63203WU, right-hand pin '1 FB', with 'R13 51.1k' to GND on the power sheet"}
      ],
      "impact": "If the FB pin is not directly on +3V3, the fixed-output buck loses its output sense and the 3.3 V rail can rise well above 3.3 V, damaging the ESP32-C3-MINI-1, the MAX31855s and the WS2812B; at minimum it puts an unintended network on the feedback node.",
      "confidence": 0.45
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["J7", "J8"],
      "pins": ["J7.1", "J7.2", "J8.1", "J8.2"],
      "nets": ["+12V"],
      "observed": "On the Power sheet the +12V rail wire at the fan headers J7 and J8 appears to reach pin 1 as well as pin 2 of each 4-pin connector, so both top pins of each header sit on +12V.",
      "expected": "The specification puts only 'the two fan-header 12 V pins (J7/J8 pin 2)' on +12V; pin 1 of each header is the fan ground return and must be on GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "the two fan-header 12 V pins (J7/J8 pin 2)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "J7/J8 Conn_01x04_Pin with the +12V wire feeding pins 1 and 2 (power sheet, right side)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The fans receive 12 V on both their supply and ground pins, so they have no return path and cannot spin; the tach outputs stay inactive and the firmware will raise fan-stall run faults.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing matches the specification in most places, but the AP63203WU feedback pin carries a 51.1 kΩ resistor (R13) to GND where the intended design ties FB directly to +3V3, and the fan headers appear to put +12V on pin 1 as well as pin 2, so at least one connectivity deviation from the specified design is present."
}

